"<strong>\"The Madelung constant is a sum over nearest neighbors.\"</strong> It counts every ion in the crystal; the nearest neighbors alone ({#} for NaCl) overestimate it by more than three times, and the sum only settles when it is added up in neutral pieces.",
"<strong>\"Electrons in a band all have the same energy.\"</strong> A band is N closely spaced levels, and the Pauli principle puts at most two electrons in each.",
"<strong>\"Metals conduct because they have more electrons.\"</strong> Magnesium and a filled band insulator can have the same number of electrons per atom; what matters is whether the highest occupied band is full, with nowhere for an electron to go.",
"<strong>\"Holes are missing atoms.\"</strong> A hole is a missing electron in an otherwise full valence band; it moves like a positive charge.",
